ight takes roughly 7 to 8.5 hours, depending on the source.\n\n**March prices:** I couldn't find fares for March 2027 specifically. Those fares aren't published far enough ahead in the pages I could read. These are the nearest figures I found:\n- **Typical round-trip economy:** Kayak puts the median at about **C$693 in January, its cheapest month**. It puts December at C$1,119 and July at C$1,081. Kayak doesn't give a March figure in the text I saw, so March is probably somewhere in between.\n- **Cheapest recent fares:** [Skyscanner](https://www.skyscanner.com/routes/yyz/lis/toronto-pearson-international-to-lisbon.html) shows C$307 one-way and C$537 return. Kayak shows economy from about C$602 round trip. These are the lowest fares seen on any date, not March fares.\n- **Cheapest airlines:** Kayak lists Air Transat (about C$609) and Porter (about C$610, with a connection) as the cheapest round-trip options over the last 5 days.\n- **TAP:** [TAP's site](https://www.flytap.com/en_us/flights-from-toronto-to-lisbon) lists round-trip fares from USD 434 in late January 2027 and USD 645 in early May 2027. It showed no March 2027 fares.\n- **Other cabins (Kayak):** premium economy from about C$1,664 and business from about C$2,602.\n\nFor March, expect roughly C$600–900 round trip in economy, which is my own estimate from the figures above. Booking about 13 weeks ahead is typically cheapest, according to Kayak, so you should book soon.\n\nI can set up a price watch for a specific March date range if you'd like. Tell me your dates and a target price."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":830,"cache_read_input_tokens":9832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5690},"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
